  "lesson": "When a constitutional transition expressly contemplates amnesty, assess it against the practical prospects of obtaining truth and reconciliation, not only the abstract availability of prosecution. Conditional amnesty may be justified where disclosure is required and the evidence needed for prosecutions is unlikely to be available, but that reasoning is specific to the transition and framework at issue.",
